    <Folder>
      <name>Intelligence Summary</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>AI Council Assessment</name>
        <styleUrl>#intel</styleUrl>
        <description>The synthesized assessment reveals a U.S. military posture characterized by sustained operational readiness across multiple domains, with notable concentrations of ISR, transport, and maritime patrol activities. Airborne operations are dominated by high-altitude ISR platforms (C560, BE20) and tanker aircraft (K35R), indicating continuous airborne support and regional contingency capabilities. The presence of Marine Corps H47 helicopters and TEX2 aircraft over key regions—including Alaska, the Gulf of Mexico, and Georgia—suggests ongoing amphibious and anti-ship training, aligning with reported maritime strike packages off Japan. Naval deployments reflect a dual focus on strategic transit and counter-narcotics operations, with USS Abraham Lincoln (CVN-72) and USS San Antonio (LPD-17) as critical assets. The increased tanker traffic through the Strait of Hormuz underscores heightened energy security concerns in the region. Additionally, the Michigan National Guard&#39;s deployment of Mark VI patrol boats in Lake Huron for Exercise Northern Strike 26-2 highlights expanding littoral and fast-attack capabilities. Overall, the data indicates a U.S. military posture emphasizing adaptive deployment strategies, regional deterrence, and readiness to address evolving global threats, with particular attention to the Pacific and Central American theaters.</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>0,0,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
